			<heading>
				Elihu Asserts God’s Justice
			</heading>
			<begin-paragraph>
			</begin-paragraph>
			<v n="1">Then Elihu answered and said :</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18034002">
			</marker>
			<v n="2">and give ear to me , you who know ;</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18034003">
			</marker>
			<v n="3">as the palate tastes food .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18034004">
			</marker>
			<v n="4">let us know among ourselves what is good .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18034005">
			</marker>
			<v n="5">and<crossref let="j" cid="c18034005.2" />God has taken away my right ;</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18034006">
			</marker>
			<v n="6">my wound is incurable , though I am<crossref let="k" cid="c18034006.1" />without transgression . ’</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18034007">
			</marker>
			<v n="7">who<crossref let="l" cid="c18034007.1" />drinks up scoffing like water ,</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18034008">
			</marker>
			<v n="8">and walks<crossref let="m" cid="c18034008.1" />with wicked men ?</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18034009">
			</marker>
			<v n="9">that he should take delight in God . ’</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18034010">
			</marker>
			<v n="10">and from the Almighty that he should do wrong .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18034011">
			</marker>
			<v n="11">and<crossref let="q" cid="c18034011.2" />according to his ways he will make it befall him .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18034012">
			</marker>
			<v n="12">and<crossref let="r" cid="c18034012.1" />the Almighty will not pervert justice .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18034013">
			</marker>
			<v n="13">and who<crossref let="s" cid="c18034013.1" />laid on him the whole world ?</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18034014">
			</marker>
			<v n="14">and<crossref let="u" cid="c18034014.2" />gather to himself his<crossref let="v" cid="c18034014.3" />spirit and his breath ,</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18034015">
			</marker>
			<v n="15">and man would<crossref let="w" cid="c18034015.1" />return to dust .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18034016">
			</marker>
			<v n="16">listen to what I say .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18034017">
			</marker>
			<v n="17">Will you condemn him who is righteous and mighty ,</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18034018">
			</marker>
			<v n="18">and to nobles , ‘ Wicked man , ’</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18034019">
			</marker>
			<v n="19">for<crossref let="b" cid="c18034019.2" />they are all the work of his hands ?</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18034020">
			</marker>
			<v n="20">and the mighty are taken away by<crossref let="e" cid="c18034020.3" />no human hand .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18034021">
			</marker>
			<v n="21">and he sees all his<crossref let="f" cid="c18034021.1" />steps .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18034022">
			</marker>
			<v n="22">where evildoers may hide themselves .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18034023">
			</marker>
			<v n="23">that he should go before God in<crossref let="i" cid="c18034023.1" />judgment .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18034024">
			</marker>
			<v n="24">and sets<crossref let="l" cid="c18034024.2" />others in their place .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18034025">
			</marker>
			<v n="25">he<crossref let="m" cid="c18034025.1" />overturns them in the night , and they are crushed .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18034026">
			</marker>
			<v n="26">in a place for all to see ,</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18034027">
			</marker>
			<v n="27">and had no regard for any of his ways ,</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18034028">
			</marker>
			<v n="28">and he<crossref let="p" cid="c18034028.2" />heard the cry of the afflicted —</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18034029">
			</marker>
			<v n="29">whether it be a nation or a man ? —</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18034030">
			</marker>
			<v n="30">that he should not ensnare the people .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18034031">
			</marker>
			<v n="31">‘ I have borne punishment ; I will not offend any more ;</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18034032">
			</marker>
			<v n="32">if I have done iniquity , I will do it no more ’ ?</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18034033">
			</marker>
			<v n="33">therefore<crossref let="s" cid="c18034033.1" />declare what you know .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18034034">
			</marker>
			<v n="34">and the wise man who hears me will say :</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18034035">
			</marker>
			<v n="35">his words are without insight . ’</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18034036">
			</marker>
			<v n="36">because he answers like wicked men .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18034037">
			</marker>
			<v n="37">and multiplies his words against God . ”</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18034038">
			</marker>
